title: 'babe: build equivocation proofs from sealed headers'
doc:
- audience:
  - Node Dev
  - Node Operator
  description: |-
    The BABE block import passed the seal-stripped pre-header to the equivocation check, so the
    equivocation proofs it generated never contained the seal and were rejected by the runtime
    with `InvalidEquivocationProof`. The check now uses the sealed header, so BABE equivocations
    are reported and slashed again.
crates:
- name: sc-consensus-babe
  bump: patch
